WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.768 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I have a child.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a child, he's two,
and I love him,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:10.210
but I have now found out that
the feeling is not mutual.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.111 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.345 line:92%
Took this boy to a fire station.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.614
He run off, start kicking it
with all the firefighters.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:18.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get it now, I get why cops
don't like firefighters.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
They got all this charisma,
firefighters.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.155 line:92%
They got all this charisma.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's nothing you can do
to stop it.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is how much we love
firefighters.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.696
Firefighters get the same amount
of hero love as cops,

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.764 line:92%
but none of the scrutiny.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
No sign of -- you've never
looked at a firefighter

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.971 size:78% position:39%
and wondered if he's
one of the good ones.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's never happened.
[ Applause ]

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.411 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey...

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.313
You want to be a good cop, you
got to hand out free ice cream.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.050
You got to go to the hood
and dance with children.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:50.650 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to be a good
firefighter,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.354
all you got to do is take your
shirt off and make a calendar.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's it.
You win the game.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.290 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't be cooler
than a firefighter.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
Only person cooler
than a firefighter

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.997 size:88% position:44% line:92%
is a forest firefighter.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's next level, 'cause they
ain't got no equipment.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:09.602
They just out in the woods with
a chainsaw and a shovel.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.737 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That's all they have.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
A chainsaw and a shovel,
chopping trees --

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.642 size:88% position:44%
It's basically CrossFit.
That's what that job is.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the X Games
of firefighting.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, oh, you like
fighting fire?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, can you do it without
a truck or water?

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:26.953 line:92%
And if that doesn't work,

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:30.156
the only thing the forest
firefighters have as backup

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.158 line:92%
is a helicopter flying overhead

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
just drizzling something
on top of the fire.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And I'm sure --

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure it's doing something.
I'm sure it's helping,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.899
but I'm watching from the house,
and I see that helicopter

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the bucket,
and it drizzles.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, that didn't do
anything at all.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
You need more helicopters.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:52.178 size:84% position:42%
Only person cooler than
a forest firefighter

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a volunteer firefighter.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.351
That's the next level, 'cause
they ain't getting no money.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.286 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.288 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No money.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
To just fight fire
on the side.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
They already have a job.
They have a job,

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.862
and then every now and then,
"Hey, man, I'll be at work,

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
"but let me know if
something burning.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm happy to swing by."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:16.136
Who you know run into a burning
building as a side hustle?

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.637 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.006 size:84% position:42%
You've got to respect
volunteer firefighters.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody loves volunteer
firefighters.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.511 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.479 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody loves a volunteer
police officer.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:33.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact, there's nothing
more scarier

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.055 line:92%
than a volunteer police --

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even the police don't trust
a volunteer --

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why they call them
vigilantes.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.231 line:92%
I have two cops in my family,

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know that one advantage
that cops for sure have

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that they get to do
their job off duty.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Off-duty cops.
Off-duty cops --

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:55.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's the only time you hear
somebody's occupation

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.076 line:92%
inserted into a news story.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do something amazing,
and it's one of us,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're just a regular --
you're just a good Samaritan.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
You ain't no
off-duty accountant.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.417 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you're a cop,
and you're a cop

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:09.289
when you didn't have to be a
cop, you're now an off-duty cop.

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:11.257
And it's always a superhero
story from an off-duty --

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:14.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
"In other news today,
an off-duty police officer,

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:18.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
he pulled a school bus from
a tornado by himself."

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.065 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The tornado has been taken
into custody."

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
Off-duty cops, 'cause cop
is the only hero job

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you can do
without equipment.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
All you need to be a cop
is courage.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.879 size:88% position:44%
You can be an off-duty
firefighter. Absolutely.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can be an off-duty
firefighter.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:35.982 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Pull up to the fire.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:39.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you do not have
your equipment,

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:42.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are just a person standing
outside of a fire.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.291
You are a bystander.
That is what you are right now.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.527 size:75% position:38%
You are a bystander.
You have no truck.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:50.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have no water.
You at the wrong fire.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.498 line:92%
You should be in the forest.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:56.669 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I get it.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:00.607
I get why these cops are jealous
of firefighters, man.

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got all this police reform
going on.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:06.679
There hasn't been a single
firefighter misconduct video.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.016 line:92%
No firefighter misconduct.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:10.850 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Plus, as a firefighter,

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's got to be hard to be
prejudiced as a firefighter.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:17.123
Half your job in the smoke,
you can't see who you're saving.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You don't know.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you a firefighter,
you trying to be prejudiced,

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:26.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
that means you got to
pat around --

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got to listen for race.
You got to hear it.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to --
"Fire Department, call out.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fire Department, you in here?
Fire Department --"

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm over here, cuz.
Save me, bruh."

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:42.148
"This floor is all clear,
headed upstairs. 10-4."

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.017 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:45.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you
to the first responders.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.786 size:78% position:39%
Thank you all so much
for having me, man.

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
Appreciate it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:51.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
